[b]Health Regen - Configurable[/b]

Human and vampire health regeneration in one configurable mod. Choose separate rates for each form, keep regeneration outside combat, or allow it during combat. Both forms default to 1.5% per second.

[b]Stops healing at the limit[/b]
Regeneration stops when your health bar or current vampire segment is full. This avoids the original vampire mod's repeated healing attempts at the limit.

[b]Configuration[/b]
[url=https://www.nexusmods.com/thebloodofdawnwalker/mods/271]Mod Settings Menu[/url] is optional. Without it, the mod uses the defaults below unless you change settings.ini manually.
[list]
[*]Human regeneration: 0% to 5% per second; default 1.5%.
[*]Vampire regeneration: 0% to 5% per second; default 1.5%.
[*]Rate steps: 0.25% from 0% through 2%, then 0.5% through 5%.
[*]Combat regeneration: Off by default. Off means outside combat only; On also allows combat regeneration.
[*]Restore vampire segments: Off by default. On allows regeneration to restore lost segments toward full health.
[*]Logging: Off by default; writes setup and aggregate diagnostics to UE4SS.log when enabled.
[/list]
Zero disables this mod's added regeneration for the selected form. Existing game regeneration bonuses remain separate. Regeneration does not revive a dead player.

[b]Manual configuration (without the menu)[/b]
Load a save once to create settings.ini, then close the game. Open this file inside your The Blood of Dawnwalker game folder:
[code]Dawnwalker\Binaries\Win64\ue4ss\Mods\HealthRegeneration\settings.ini[/code]
The default settings are:
[code][Settings]
vampireRegenPercent = 1.5
humanRegenPercent = 1.5
combatRegen = 0
restoreVampireSegments = 0
debugLogging = 0[/code]
Change either regeneration rate using the steps above; 1.5 means 1.5% per second. For combatRegen, restoreVampireSegments and debugLogging, use 0 for Off or 1 for On. Save the file, restart the game and load a save to apply your changes.

[b]Installation[/b]
[list]
[*]Vortex: Install Health-Regen-Configurable.zip through Vortex, enable it and deploy.
[*]Manual: Copy the archive's Dawnwalker folder into ...\steamapps\common\The Blood of Dawnwalker\, preserving the folder structure.
[/list]

[b]Credits and source[/b]
